From 2b85b0b269bad6ae8f98e4059a72aba4f00c9f6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:08:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kk: fix audit robustness findings (XFB bounds, sparse
 container_of, minmax UAB scan, sparse view offset)

Five confirmed audit findings in the KosmicKrisp patches:

- kk_cmd_draw.c (0010): kk_begin_end_xfb indexed params.src[idx] with
  idx = first_counter + i, unbounded, into libkk_xfb_counter_copy's fixed
  src[4]/dest[4]; a guest firstCounterRange past POLY_MAX_SO_BUFFERS wrote
  past the host stack. Skip such indices.
- nir_to_msl.c (0027): the assert guarding container_of(src, nir_alu_src,
  src) is compiled out with -Db_ndebug=true, so a non-ALU user of a sparse
  fetch's def produced a bogus nir_alu_src and out-of-bounds swizzle
  writes. Skip non-ALU users instead.
- kk_shader.c (0036): the reduce-sampler scan broke out as soon as any set
  needed minmax, so update-after-bind sets scanned later were never
  recorded in minmax_uab_sets; a reduction sampler they got after
  recording went unnoticed and stale plain-program results were drawn.
  Scan every such set (a one-time-submit command buffer still uses the
  minmax program right away).
- kk_image.c (0019): pPlaneLayouts[0] was dereferenced before the check
  that drmFormatModifierPlaneCount is 1, so a guest explicit create info
  with no plane layouts read through a NULL pointer. Check the count and
  the pointer first.
- kk_sparse.c (0031): page_count - first_page underflowed when a buffer
  view's offset was past the buffer, and MIN2 kept the view's own size,
  mapping texels beyond the buffer. Clamp to zero pages.

Generated-by: LLM
